  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the product rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡a+{log}_{n}⁡b={log}_{n}⁡(ab)\n$$\n\nIf we factor the given expression and use the product rule for logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{ln}⁡p+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡q+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(pq) & =5(\\operatorname{ln}⁡p+\\operatorname{ln}⁡q+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(pq)) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(p\\cdot q\\cdot pq) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡({p}^{2}{q}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
